SPOILERS

ok, let's see which items you will actually need:

- amulet of life saving
you should become able to protect your life. an amulet will do this
only once.

- decent blessed rustproof weapon
the tsurugi of muramasa is actually the best. you can wield it only
when you are either lawful or a samurai. it's a two-handed weapon, so
you can't wear a silver shield.
mjollnir and frost brand come close to this one.

- rustproof speed boots
really essential.

- silver shield
as long as you don't have sleep, fire and cold resistance or aren't
extremely lucky you need it.

- gray dragon scale mail
magic resistance isn't that important in the beginning and you might
get it by other means (cloak of mag.res., some of the quest items).
usually you will find a dwarvish mithril coat which just has 3 AC
points less than GDSM. So it would be even more reasonable to wish for
a blessed magic marker and write some scrolls of enchant armor.

- gauntlets of power
very good when playing a character with low strength.

- helm of opposite alignment
you won't really need it in the beginning.

- cloak of displacement
nice but not essential.

- ring of regeneration
you should be able to survive without one.

- ring of conflict
nice but not too essential.

- ring of teleport control
better eat a tengu. as long as you don't have teleport intrinsic it's
not too useful and with all those wands and scrolls of teleportation
you won't need this intrinsic too much.

- ring of increase damage
good to have in the end (what else should you put on your
ring-fingers?). first write your scrolls of enchant weapon.

- unicorn horn
wish for cursed scrolls of genocide instead (or a cursed magic marker
when you already know how to write them) and reverse genocide unicorns
of a different color. get poison resistance by eating them.

- blessed bag of holding
you will find one.

- blessed platinum yendorian express card
one of my favorites. gives tou mag.res. and ESP. works like a blessed
scroll of charging when you invoke it. you must be either neutral or a
tourist in order to carry it.

- ring of levitation
not too important in the beginning.

- blessed luckstone
there's always one in the gnomish mines.

you are going to find all the different useful wands. also I wouldn't
go for spellbooks - the only spell that might be useful to survive is
the charm monster spell. reading spellbooks is risky for stupid
characters.

usually my first wish is for a blessed figurine of an archon. the
archon will drop a silver shield and a blessed rustproof named weapon
(most of the times sunsword or demonbane) and is probably the best
pet, also because s/he doesn't eat. guide her/him to down to mine town
and let her kill all the shopkeepers. with their gold buy protection
from the temple priestess. let the archon kill her, too and get the
spellbooks she was carrying. sometimes she was also wearing a cloak of
mag.res. go to the bottom of the mines and get the luckstone there.
back to the temple and start sacrificing. use the fountains in mine
town and let the archon kill the angry watchmen. win this game.



